From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Fuchs <contact@fuchskurt.eu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:04:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] core: add enforce-secure-boot locked policy

Image verification in LoadImage and the direct-Linux guard no longer depend
on the mutable SecureBoot/SecureBootEnable state when the feature is set.
Default Microsoft keys are never auto-enrolled, disabling Secure Boot and
clearing keys are refused, the Secure Boot setup menu is compiled out, and
boot halts unless the persisted PK puts the platform in User Mode with
Secure Boot enabled.

The setup-only PK deletion behind clear-all also refuses in this build, so
no future caller can reach it, and turning the SecureBootEnable preference
off (directly or through the toggle) fails with ACCESS_DENIED.
---
